# modules.cpp bitmap font module

# Status and authority

status: official gives the implemented portions of this document the same
authority as the other v1.2.1 specifications. This document specifies the
implemented mm.fonts module: the Glyph, Font, and TextMetrics types, the
measure, render, and expand_row functions, and the committed kMono12 and
kMono16 glyph tables derived from IBM Plex Mono. The font-demo application
exists. Legible text on a physical panel remains a hardware-qualification
requirement rather than a completed claim.

docs/modules-display.mdy owns the portable display boundary and its pixel
packing. docs/modules-platform-mcu.mdy owns the MCU provider model. mm.fonts
sits above mm.display and consumes nothing below it, and this document must
not weaken either boundary to make one panel draw text quickly.

# Role

mm.fonts turns a UTF-8 string into exactly the packed bytes mm.display
writes. mm.display moves packed pixels and names the boundary in its own
manifest: graphics policy, fonts, image decoding, and controller commands
live above or below it, not inside it. Text support is the layer that closes
that gap for the two panels this project targets, the 152 by 296 one-bit
ePaper and the 240 by 320 sixteen-bit RGB565 LCD.

The module obeys the standing project rules:

- No vector parsing and no font engine on the target. The bitmaps are
  precomputed at development time and shipped as static data.
- No heap at runtime. Every structure is a span over provider-owned static
  storage that outlives its users, the same shape the display drivers use
  for their initialization tables.
- One portable sequence for both panels. Text is composed into a one-bit
  frame; the one-bit panel receives those rows, and the sixteen-bit panel
  receives each row expanded to RGB565.
- Monospace by design. A fixed cell width makes wrapping and alignment
  arithmetic, which is what a terminal-style panel UI wants.

# IBM Plex Mono

The committed tables are derived from IBM Plex Mono, IBM's monospace
typeface, licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 (OFL). The OFL is an
open source font licence, copyright 2017 IBM Corp., with the reserved font
name "Plex". Its terms that reach this project:

- It permits use, study, copy, merge, embed, modify, redistribution, and
  sale of modified and unmodified copies.
- The font software may not be sold by itself, which firmware never does.
- Every distributed copy carries the copyright notice and the licence. The
  repository carries the OFL text at modules/mm/fonts/licenses/OFL.txt
  beside the Apache 2.0 root licence, and each generated table names its
  provenance in a header comment.
- The reserved name "Plex" may not be the primary user-facing name of a
  derivative work. The module keeps "Plex" to provenance attribution and
  keeps its identifiers neutral, kMono12 and kMono16 rather than kPlex12.

The face facts the module relies on:

- Coverage: 1049 glyphs, unitsPerEm 1000, all 95 printable ASCII code points,
  and all 18 Polish letters, ą ć ę ł ń ó ś ź ż in both cases.
- Monospacing: every printable-ASCII advance is exactly 600 units, 0.600 em.
  The face is a true monospace, which is what a fixed-cell display UI wants.
- Format: vector outlines only. IBM ships no bitmap variant, which is why the
  module's bitmaps are generated from the TTF at development time instead of
  parsed at runtime.

